{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification encodes a conservative, coverage-oriented supervisor: in clear/search states, random_walk is preferred for exploration; move_forward is used in a dedicated short-commit state. Obstacle events force explicit, one-shot recovery turns away from the blocked side, never enabling forward or random_walk in obstacle states. Recovery states are exited only after a turn, and path_clear returns the robot to exploration. Full_rotate is reserved for the rare case of being blocked on all sides. All transitions are deterministic and safe.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect hardware modularity.",
    "Specification automaton encodes a compact, deterministic supervisor: random_walk in clear/search, move_forward in commit, explicit turn recovery for obstacles, and rapid return to exploration after path_clear."
  ],
